# Architecture

```
src/
  main.rs              # thin entrypoint
  lib.rs               # module root and public re-exports
  presentation/        # cli.rs — argv, file open, exit codes
  application/         # process_transactions.rs — read → apply → write
  domain/              # transaction, account, ledger — all business rules
  infrastructure/      # csv.rs — serde row types, parse/write helpers
```

## Dependency rule

`presentation → application → domain ← infrastructure`

- **Domain** depends on nothing external (no `std::io`, no `serde`, no `csv`)
- **Application** orchestrates streaming via `Read` / `Write`; signature: `run<R: Read, W: Write>(input: R, output: W) -> Result<(), AppError>`
- **Infrastructure** owns CSV parsing/serialization; depends only on domain types
- **Presentation** wires CLI to application and infrastructure

## Data flow

1. CLI parses `argv[1]` as input path
2. `CsvTransactionReader` streams `Transaction` rows
3. `ProcessTransactions` applies each row to `Ledger`
4. On EOF, `Ledger` produces account snapshots
5. `CsvAccountWriter` serializes to stdout

## Anti-patterns

```rust
// ❌ Domain importing I/O or serde
use csv::Reader;
use serde::Deserialize;

// ❌ Business rules in presentation or infrastructure
fn parse_and_apply_deposit(row: &str) { /* balance logic here */ }

// ✅ Domain pure logic; infrastructure adapts I/O
ledger.apply(&transaction);
```
